<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine (film, John Lennon and Yoko Ono)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1972</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the song opens the 81-minute film of the album</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Come from the Shadows (Joan Baez)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1972</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Touch Me in the Morning (Diana Ross)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1973</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine There's No Pizza (Herman Cain)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1991</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Other Side of Summer (Elvis Costello)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1991</span><span class="sg-chain-h">answer song (echoes the criticism of a rich star singing of no possessions)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Working Class Hero: A Tribute to John Lennon (Blues Traveler)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1995</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine (Eva Cassidy)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Imagine Project (Herbie Hancock, with Seal, Pink, India.Arie, Jeff Beck and others)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2010</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover; Grammy for Best Pop Vocal Collaboration, 2011</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine (UNICEF initiative for the Convention on the Rights of the Child)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2014</span><span class="sg-chain-h">covers in a sing-along app</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine (Yoko Ono)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2018</span><span class="sg-chain-h">solo recording by the co-writer</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine (Julian Lennon)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2022</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover, for refugees of the war in Ukraine</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Imagine (music video by Zbigniew Rybczyński)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1986</span><span class="sg-chain-h">music video; Silver Lion at Cannes, 1987</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Cloud Piece, in Grapefruit (Yoko Ono)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1964</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the concept and much of the lyric, by Lennon's account</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Christian prayer book given by Dick Gregory</span><span class="sg-chain-h">idea of positive prayer, by Lennon's account</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">John's Piano Piece (Let It Be sessions)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">early form of the piano motif</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Saying of Lillian Piché Shirt's grandmother</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969 (radio conversation)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">possible source, argued by Sarah Carter</span></li></ul></section>
